    "flow_description": "## Model Flow Description\n\nThis model processes data through the following stages:\n\n### Stage 1: Feature Extraction\n\n- **conv1** (Conv): applies a [3, 3] convolution with 1 groups, producing ? feature maps\n\n### Stage 2: Activation\n\n- **relu1** (Relu): applies ReLU activation, zeroing negative values to introduce non-linearity\n\n### Stage 3: Feature Extraction\n\n- **conv2** (Conv): applies a [3, 3] convolution with 1 groups, producing ? feature maps\n\n### Stage 4: Activation\n\n- **relu2** (Relu): applies ReLU activation, zeroing negative values to introduce non-linearity\n\n### Stage 5: Spatial Reduction\n\n- **maxpool** (MaxPool): downsamples by taking maximum values in [2, 2] regions\n\n### Stage 6: Feature Extraction\n\n- **conv3** (Conv): applies a [3, 3] convolution with 1 groups, producing ? feature maps\n\n### Stage 7: Activation\n\n- **relu3** (Relu): applies ReLU activation, zeroing negative values to introduce non-linearity\n\n### Stage 8: Spatial Reduction\n\n- **gap** (GlobalAveragePool): collapses spatial dimensions by global averaging, preparing for classification\n\n### Stage 9: Tensor Reshaping\n\n- **flatten** (Flatten): reshapes multi-dimensional features into a flat vector\n"
